{"type": "thinking", "text": "Interesting! Tablet strength 50 carried over to Capsule strength 50! So cross-form carry-over DOES work here (Tablet → Capsule within Antiandrogen). But earlier Tablet→Injection did not. Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the carry-over works only when both forms share the same field type/unit (mg strength). Tablet strength (mg) → Capsule strength (mg) both \"strength mg\". Injection \"Vial strength (mg)\" is also mg strength though. Why didn't 3 carry? Hmm, maybe because the two forms are within the same category? Tablet and Capsule are both in Antiandrogen. Injection is Estradiol category. Wait, category was Estradiol at that time too (Estradiol category includes Tablet, Injection, Gel, Patch). The form change Tablet→Injection stayed in Estradiol category.\n\nHmm, but here Tablet→Capsule carried over 50. And notably, \"Capsule strength (mg)\" is the same amount field semantics. So carry-over works for mg strength field. But Injection's \"Vial strength (mg)\" didn't get 3? Odd. Let me retest: Maybe there's something where Injection form is different because it goes through \"Preparation type\" screen? Wait, injection showed \"Preparation type: Ampule/Vial\" and \"Vial strength (mg)\". Hmm.\n\nAlso interesting: when I first opened Add medicine (Estradiol tablet), the tablet strength was empty. Fine.\n\nWait, actually maybe the carry-over happened because 50 was typed in Tablet and when switching to Capsule, capsule's \"strength\" state was initialized from the tablet's strength — because the *form picker* copies amount fields that are compatible. Injection's field might have a different internal id (vial strength) though still mg.\n\nHmm, let me check: When switching Tablet→Injection earlier, tablet strength was \"3\", injection showed empty. So no carry to injection. When Tablet→Capsule, 50 carried. So inconsistent. Possibly a bug specific to some forms. The changed note says \"every amount field is now carried over when the form is changed\" — implying all forms. So injection might be the bug.\n\nBut careful: maybe the order matters: I typed 50 in Tablet while... hmm, in the tablet→injection case I had typed 3 and the keyboard was still shown; then I tapped Injection directly while the keyboard was up. Did that matter? In the tablet→capsule case I pressed BACK first then tapped Capsule. Maybe the field state wasn't committed when switching with keyboard open? But the field is a state-backed text field; tapping another element should commit.\n\nLet me retest Tablet→Injection carefully with keyboard dismissed: currently Capsule with 50. Switch to Tablet, check 50 still there, dismiss keyboard, switch to Injection, check.\n\nNow the category is Antiandrogen; Injection isn't available in Antiandrogen. Let me switch category to Estradiol first, then form Tablet, enter value, then Injection.\n\nActually, easier: switch category to Estradiol. What happens to form selection and amounts? Let me tap Estradiol category."}
