{"type": "thinking", "text": "Confirmed again: Tablet strength 3 → Injection \"Vial strength (mg)\" empty. So the carry-over works for Tablet→Capsule within Antiandrogen but not Tablet→Injection within Estradiol. Interesting.\n\nHmm wait. Maybe the difference: In Antiandrogen, switching to Capsule also changed the medication to Dutasteride (because Spironolactone doesn't have a capsule form?). The carry-over of \"50\" might actually be because the capsule's strength state is shared with the tablet strength? Hmm.\n\nLet me think about implementation. Probably a shared \"amount\" state per form field role, e.g. field \"strength\" (mg), \"concentration\", \"totalAmount\". Tablet strength and Capsule strength are both \"strength\". Injection vial strength is also \"strength\" though...\n\nWait, maybe the difference is: In the Injection form, the \"Vial strength\" is shown only when \"Preparation type=Vial\", default is Ampule. When Ampule selected, maybe the amount field is a different one (\"Ampule strength\"?). But the displayed field says \"Vial strength (mg)\" even with Ampule checked. Hmm, weird: \"Ampule\" checked but field label \"Vial strength (mg)\". That might itself be a minor inconsistency.\n\nMaybe there's a separate amount field for Ampule hidden? Actually the form shows one amount field \"Vial strength (mg)\" and preset 5 mg/10 mg. The default preparation type is Ampule. Confusing but okay.\n\nLet me test Injection→Gel carry-over: currently Injection, enter 10, then switch to Gel. Gel currently has 0.1/80 retained from before. If carry-over works, gel fields might become 10 and something. Let's test after entering 10.\n\nActually hold on. Let me reconsider the note: \"Preparation form picker: every amount field is now carried over when the form is changed.\" Perhaps the *real* bug being fixed was: when switching form, the values of the amount fields in the OLD form should be carried over to the new form's same-named fields. But my observations suggest cross-form carry only happened Tablet→Capsule. Let me test Injection with 10→Vial toggle→Ampule etc.\n\nLet me be systematic with a table:\n\nForms in Estradiol category: Tablet (Tablet strength mg), Injection (Preparation type: Ampule/Vial; Vial strength mg), Gel (Preparation type: Container/Sachet; Gel concentration %, Total gel amount g), Patch (Patch specification: Total dose/Release rate; Total amount in patch mg / Patch release rate μg/day).\n\nLet me enter values in each and test switching around. Current: Injection. Type 10 in Vial strength. Then switch to Gel → observe gel values (previously 0.1/80). Then back to Injection → see if 10 kept. Then switch to Patch, observe. Then to Tablet, observe (3?).\n\nLet me do it."}
