{"type": "thinking", "text": "Very interesting! When switching \"Preparation type\" from Ampule to Vial, the fields change:\n- Ampule: \"Vial strength (mg)\" (single field)\n- Vial: \"Concentration (mg/mL)\" and \"Vial volume (mL)\" (two fields)\n\nAnd the amount \"10\" typed in Ampule's field is NOT carried over to Vial's fields (both empty). That's a carry-over failure across the preparation type, not form. But the changelog says \"Preparation form picker: every amount field is now carried over when the form is changed\" — hmm, \"preparation form\" here could indeed be interpreted as the \"Preparation form\" picker (Tablet/Injection/Gel/Patch), not \"Preparation type\".\n\nBUT: notice the Ampule option's field label is \"Vial strength (mg)\". That seems like a bug: Ampule should have \"Ampule strength (mg)\" perhaps. Wait, is it possible the app shows \"Vial strength (mg)\" for Ampule because... hmm. Let me look at the screenshot of the earlier state to verify. The observation said \"Vial strength (mg)\". Yes. And the presets 5 mg/10 mg — typical ampule doses of estradiol valerate (5mg, 10mg). \"Vial\" often holds 20mg/mL etc. So probably a labeling bug: under \"Ampule\" the field is labeled \"Vial strength (mg)\". Hmm, maybe intentional? \"Vial strength\" for ampule doesn't make sense.\n\nThis could be a genuine bug but may be outside the scope (injection form fields). The task area is \"adding medicines: categories and preparation forms\", so it is in scope.\n\nBut first, the key changelog item. Let me test the Vial sub-type: enter concentration 40, volume 10, then switch back to Ampule — does anything carry to \"Vial strength (mg)\"? Then switch back to Vial: do both values return?\n\nLet me do it. Type 40 in concentration (element 16)."}
