he dose it shows is now looked up across all of the day's schedule slots\" suggests the card looks up the dose from the day's schedule (each slot may have a dose), and previously it looked only at the first slot (maybe the morning slot) so if the first slot had no dose or a different dose, the displayed dose was wrong.\n\nHow can a slot have a different dose? In this app, a group has a set of medications with per-dose counts, and times. All slots in a group have the same meds. But you can have multiple groups containing the same medicine with different doses. Or a medication can be in multiple groups. Then on a given day, there could be several schedule slots for the same antiandrogen with possibly different doses. The card should look up the dose across all slots (e.g., the next upcoming, or the maximum?).\n\nHmm, to test this, I'd need two groups: one with a low dose at an earlier/later slot and one with a high dose. E.g., Group A (Estradiol only) and Group B (Spironolactone 1 tablet at 10PM). Hmm.\n\nActually maybe there's a simpler interpretation: The card shows the dose for the *next due* slot. The bug being fixed: when the next due slot doesn't include the medicine, the card showed the dose from a slot that wasn't relevant. Whatever.\n\nSince this is a \"changed in this build\" item, likely the build has a bug in this feature. Let me try to construct a scenario where the dose differs across slots.\n\nPlan: Create a second group \"Night\" containing Spironolactone with different tablets-per-dose (e.g., 2 tablets = 100 mg) at 11:00 PM only. Then Home antiandrogen card should show? Maybe \"50 mg\" or \"100 mg\". Hmm, hard to know expected.\n\nAlternatively, the card might show a dose like \"2 tablets\". Let me examine the card's data sources. The card row: \"Oral · Spironolactone\" title, subtitle \"Oral · 50 mg\". Wait, \"Oral · 50 mg\" — maybe \"Oral\" is the med form/route and \"50 mg\" is the dose *per intake* (1 tablet × 50 mg). With Count=1, tablets per dose = 1 → 50 mg.\n\nIf I create a group with Spironolactone at 2 tablets per dose, the card might show \"Oral · 100 mg\". Then with two groups (50mg at 10PM, 100mg at 11PM) the card should show... the next due? This would test the \"across all slots\" lookup.\n\nBut wait: the current group already has Spironolactone with \"Tablets per dose\" fraction 1 and Count 1. The group row showed \"Oral · 50 mg\". So the dose per intake is 50 mg.\n\nHmm, what if I change the group's spironolactone to 1/2 tablet? Then the row would show \"Oral · 25 mg\"? Let's see. That would confirm the \"dose\" is derived from the schedule entry.\n\nActually, let me look at the group's medication row: the element was \"Oral | Spironolactone | Oral · 50 mg\". Maybe the second \"Oral · 50 mg\" is the dosage presentation (route · strength) from the medicine itself, and the count isn't shown. Hmm.\n\nLet me tap the group's Spironolactone row in the editor to see its edit sheet and what dose info it shows.\n\nBefore that, let's note the card currently shows \"Last dose 0m ago\" (after logging). Let me check what it shows when a dose is due soon (e.g., 10PM). Not critical.\n\nLet me look at the card's \"dose\" from a different angle: maybe the card is supposed to show \"50 mg\" as the *daily total* across slots. The group has 4 slots per day each with 50 mg → 200 mg/day. But the card shows 50 mg. Hmm, so no.\n\nActually, maybe \"the dose it shows\" refers to the *antiandrogen card's subtitle*, e.g., \"Oral · 50 mg\". And the lookup across slots relates to which medication entry is shown when the same antiandrogen appears in multiple schedule slots with different doses. Eh.\n\nLet me not over-theorize. Let me test the other areas and see if more concrete bugs emerge. Then decide about the Home card.\n\nWait, actually — maybe the antiandrogen card is supposed to show the *next scheduled dose and time*. Note before logging it showed \"No logged dose yet | Due 10:00 PM\". After logging at 3:12PM (early),