{"type": "thinking", "text": "Interesting: the Injection form now retained 10 from before! Earlier I thought Injection was empty after switching. Now it shows 10. So per-form memory works for Injection too. Hmm, in the earlier clean test, Injection was empty on first visit (never entered). Now it retains 10 from the earlier entry. That's consistent with per-form memory.\n\nSo \"every amount field is now carried over when the form is changed\" = per-form values are retained. It works. The switching does not copy values between forms, but it retains each form's own. Given the changelog wording, \"carried over\" might mean the draft values persist. Hmm. But then why would \"every amount field\" matter? Because a form like Gel has 2 amount fields; both persist. That's plausible as a fix.\n\nOK, so maybe there's NO bug in the prep form carry-over, and it works. Hmm.\n\nLet me test the specific \"every amount field\" scenario: set Gel's two fields, switch away, back → both retained (works). Set Injection Vial's two fields, switch away, back → both retained? Let's test: Vial sub-type with concentration 40, volume 10. Switch to Gel, then back to Injection (should still be Vial with both values). Then switch prep type to Ampule and back to Vial → both retained? Earlier when switching Vial→Ampule→Vial, 40/10 were retained. Yes.\n\nBut there's a cross-field oddity: switching Vial→Ampule gave Ampule field \"10\" (from Vial's volume). That's the \"carry-over\" between preparation types. Maybe the \"Preparation form picker\" change is actually about the \"Preparation type\" picker (Ampule/Vial). The section in the UI is labeled \"Preparation form\" for the outer picker and \"Preparation type\" for the inner. The changelog says \"Preparation form picker\" — outer. Hmm.\n\nBut wait: the Ampule field showing 10 after Vial→Ampule is suspicious. Let's reproduce cleanly: \n1. Currently Injection/Ampule with 10.\n2. Tap Vial. The fields: concentration and volume — what do they show? Earlier they had 40/10. Let me check.\n3. If concentration=40, volume=10: tap Ampule → check strength (probably 10).\nThis indicates the carry-over maps the *second* amount field of Vial (volume) into the single Ampule field, ignoring the first (concentration). If the changelog says \"every amount field is now carried over\", maybe the intended result is that the Ampule field gets... hmm.\n\nActually, maybe the intended semantics is: switching prep type carries the *last edited* amount field. The last edited was volume 10 → Ampule strength 10. That's reasonable! The \"amount\" (last value) is carried over. So Ampule gets 10.\n\nHmm, then in Tablet→Injection Ampule, the last edited amount was Tablet strength 2 → Ampule should get 2, but it's empty (first visit to Injection). So cross-form doesn't carry. But cross-prep-type does.\n\nOK, I'm now fairly convinced the \"carry over\" is per-form/per-type state retention, and it works. The changelog might be describing the fix for a bug where changing the form lost values, and this build has the fix. Good.\n\nBut wait, one thing: when switching from Gel to Patch earlier, the Patch's Total amount field was empty (never entered). Fine.\n\nLet me now test an important edge: switch form with unsaved *typed* value (keyboard open) — does it retain? Let me do:\n- Currently Injection/Ampule with 10, keyboard dismissed.\n- Tap the strength field, type 55 (appends if not cleared? use clear). Then WITHOUT dismissing keyboard, tap Tablet. Then return to Injection: is the value 55 or 10?\nThis tests \"amount carried over when form changed\" with uncommitted input. If it loses 55 → real bug (typing lost on form change).\n\nLet me do it."}
