n the three areas. Maybe I've missed something.\n\nLet me re-examine the group editor schedule section for subtler bugs:\n- The count \"TIMES OF DAY · N\" updates correctly.\n- The times are ordered.\n- What about *saving* the group with times in order: the Plan row shows \"12:00 AM/8:00 AM/10:00 PM/11:00 PM\" — sorted.\n- The Plan group row lists times separated by \"/\" — fine.\n\nWhat about the \"Weekly\" schedule? Switching to Weekly might reveal day-of-week selection. The ordering of reminder times may break when Weekly. Let me check Group 2 (editable) → Weekly → add times. Hmm.\n\nAnother possible bug: In the \"Add group\" editor, the default time 3:30 PM is set, but if you add a second time and then delete the first (Remove), does the count update and ordering hold? Let me test Remove: Group 2 has one time 9:00 PM. Add a time 7:00 AM, then edit 9:00 PM and Remove it, leaving 7:00 AM. Check count. Also test removing all times — can you save with 0 times? That might be a valid bug (schedule with no times). Let me test.\n\nActually, a schedule group with zero times is invalid; if the app allows saving it, that's a bug (doses never occur). Let me test: create Group 3 with a medication, remove the only time, then see if Save is enabled and whether saving works. That's a good edge case (\"Input: try empty\").\n\nLet me do it. Currently the Add medicine sheet is open in landscape with a scrolled state. Cancel it. Then add a group with medication, remove all times, try Save.\n\nSteps:\n1. Rotate to portrait (cleaner).\n2. Cancel sheet.\n3. Plan → Add group.\n4. Add Spironolactone (or estradiol).\n5. Tap the time chip → Remove.\n6. Check TIMES OF DAY count and Save enabled.\n7. Try Save; observe result.\n\nLet me do it."}
