{"type": "thinking", "text": "Hmm, this time the edit dialog has no \"Remove\" button (because it's the only time — removing the only time might be disallowed, or the dialog varies). Earlier when editing one of three times, there was a Remove button. For the only time, there's no Remove. That's a sensible safeguard. Good — no bug there.\n\nSo no empty-times save possible. Let me Cancel the dialog (element 21) and cancel the group.\n\nNow let me investigate the prep-form carry-over more. I need to decide. Let me think about what the \"carry over\" feature would be from the app's design. The Add Medicine form likely persists per-form values via a state map keyed by form type. When you change the form, the values are \"carried over\" — maybe to the new form's fields when the form has the same fields? Hmm.\n\nActually — new idea: maybe \"carried over\" refers to the **preset selection**. When you select a preset amount (e.g., \"2 mg\"), then change the form, the preset amount carries over. We tested presets: Tablet 2 mg → Gel empty. So no.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the carry-over is between the \"Preparation type\" options within a form (Ampule/Vial, Container/Sachet, Total dose/Release rate). We saw Vial→Ampule carried 10 (the volume). Let me test Container→Sachet for Gel: set Container concentration 0.3, total 80, switch to Sachet — what happens? Sachet might have different fields (e.g., \"Sachet strength (g)\"?). The changed note says \"Preparation form picker: every amount field is now carried over when the form is changed.\" Hmm. \"Preparation form picker\" could refer to the picker that selects the *form* (Tablet/Injection/Gel/Patch), and \"form\" could loosely include the sub-type.\n\nLet me test Gel Container→Sachet to see the fields and values. This is in scope (preparation forms). Currently the Add-medicine sheet is not open; I cancelled? No, I'm in the time dialog. Let me cancel it and the group, then open Add medicine.\n\nActually, I realize I should test the Sachet sub-type anyway for coverage. Let me do that.\n\nCancel the time dialog (element 21), then Cancel group (element 19)."}
