{"type": "thinking", "text": "Switching Gel Container→Sachet:\n- Gel concentration (%) carried over 0.3. ✓\n- The second field changed from \"Total gel amount (g)\" to \"Amount per sachet (g)\" and is EMPTY (80 not carried). ✗\n\nThis is the \"every amount field is carried over when the form is changed\" claim — here the second amount field did NOT carry over: \"Total gel amount (g)\" 80 → \"Amount per sachet (g)\" empty. This looks like a concrete bug matching the changelog! And it's within the Gel form's preparation type switch (Container→Sachet). Hmm, but the changelog says \"Preparation form picker\" (outer). Still, this is an amount field not carrying over when the form/prep type changed.\n\nAlso note: the first field (concentration) carried 0.3, the second didn't. \"every amount field is now carried over\" — the second isn't. That's a strong, specific bug: when switching the Gel preparation type from Container to Sachet, the \"Total gel amount (g)\" value 80 is not carried to \"Amount per sachet (g)\"; only the concentration carries.\n\nWait, are the fields semantically the same? \"Total gel amount (g)\" (total container content) vs \"Amount per sachet (g)\" (per-sachet content) — not exactly. But the changelog says every amount field carries over. And the field positions match. The first carried. Hmm, the mismatch in unit/semantics might be intentional (no carry for per-sachet). But then why does the concentration carry?\n\nAlso consider: presets changed from \"80g\" to \"0.5g/1.0g/1.25g/2.5g\". So the second field is a different quantity. The first (concentration) is shared and carried.\n\nHmm, maybe the intended fix is exactly this: carry over amount values where fields are \"the same\". The second field is not the same → no carry. So maybe it's intended.\n\nArgh.\n\nLet me switch back to Container and see: does concentration 0.3 stay and the total gel amount 80 restore? Earlier we saw the per-type values are retained. Let me check."}
