{"type": "thinking", "text": "Reproduced cleanly: On the Custom category, selecting μg then switching the preparation form Tablet→Capsule resets the unit to mg (even with no value entered). So the unit is not carried across form change. This is a real, reproducible bug.\n\nThe dev said \"could not reproduce with the steps given.\" Maybe the steps were not precise enough (I didn't mention Custom + selecting μg before switching; actually I did mention Category: Custom and Unit μg). Hmm. Or maybe the dev needs a different phrasing. Let me re-file with more precise steps and the exact quote.\n\nNote: my earlier report's expected/observed mentioned \"50 μg becomes 50 mg\". The repro without a value shows the unit reset even before entering a value. Let me report the simpler, undeniable observation: unit selection resets.\n\nBut is this \"wrong_value\"? The unit is a setting; resetting it is a state-carry failure. Could use \"not_persisted\"? The symptom types: wrong_value, missing, not_persisted, cut_off, wrong_navigation, no_effect, duplicated, overlap. The unit reset when switching form is a \"not_persisted\" or \"wrong_value\". I think \"wrong_value\" fits: the unit shown (mg) is wrong relative to the user's selection (μg). Let me use wrong_value.\n\nElement ref: latest observe element 13 \"Capsule strength (mg)\" or element 15 \"mg\" checked. Use 13, quote \"Capsule strength (mg)\".\n\nSteps:\n1. Plan > Medicines > Add medicine.\n2. Category: Custom (preparation form Tablet default).\n3. Tap the μg unit chip (strength label becomes \"Tablet strength (μg)\").\n4. Tap Preparation form: Capsule.\n5. Observe the unit: mg is checked and the field label is \"Capsule strength (mg)\".\n\nExpected: the selected unit (μg) should be carried over, label \"Capsule strength (μg)\".\nObserved: unit resets to mg.\n\nLet me file."}
