duled dose* (e.g., 100 mg for 2 tablets). We observe it shows \"100 mg\" for group 2. That's likely the fix working! Yes — the group 2 row shows \"2 tablets · 100 mg\", which comes from the schedule. So the lookup works.\n\nSo what's the bug? Perhaps when the *same medicine* is in two slots with different doses, the card should show... hmm, it shows both. \n\nWait, maybe the card is supposed to show only ONE row per medicine and the duplicate row IS the bug. Let me test with a *single* group with two time slots and see if the card shows one or two rows. Currently group 1 has 4 times but the card shows ONE row for group 1 (not one per time) — so the card dedupes slots and shows per group. Good. With two groups, two rows. Could be intended.\n\nHmm, let me look at the card's layout: it's a single card \"Antiandrogen\" containing multiple medicine rows. If the app shows one row per group, that's a design choice (each group is a regimen). The plan has \"2 GROUPS · 2 DAILY\". The card shows both groups. Reasonable.\n\nOK, maybe the Home card bug is more subtle: the \"Due\" time. Group 1's row says \"Due 10:00 PM\". Group 2's row says \"Due 9:00 PM\". Wait, I logged the group 1 10PM dose early (at 3:12PM), which didn't count. So due 10PM is right.\nBut hold on: the group 1 row shows \"Last dose 13m ago\" and \"Due 10:00 PM\"; the group 2 row \"No logged dose yet\" and \"Due 9:00 PM\". Fine.\n\nNow, what if I log the 9PM group 2 dose (early)? It would show \"Last dose...\" and due maybe tomorrow. Fine.\n\nLet me look at the UPCOMING section: earlier initially \"Nothing scheduled in the next 90 days.\" Now there should be upcoming items. Let me scroll to the bottom of Home to see UPCOMING. Earlier (before groups) the bottom showed TOMORROW. Let me scroll down and check the UPCOMING section for duplicates/overlaps or wrong dates."}
